# harmony-closure.rows — vendor-official.sh CLOSURE base assignment (the
# web-boot closure copy list), machine-spliced by
# gen-staging-emit-closure.mjs; the staging-generated gate fails on drift.
# A literal row is policy: it must exist under runtime/dsh (the copy
# source). An `@walk` line is a find-span position, recomputed from the
# materialized pin trees at check/emit time — a new vendored file joins
# ONLY via `node tools/gen-staging-emit.mjs --emit tools/generated/staging`
# + commit (the find's automaticity is gone by design: the flip contract).
# The pre-flip $PIN interpolation is expanded: a pin bump is a row edit in
# the same commit as the script's PIN= line.
